# Build context trim for `docker build -f docker/Dockerfile .` (root context, whole reactor).
#
# docker/Dockerfile deliberately does `COPY . .` rather than listing modules: the reactor builds
# workspace-daemon's dependencies from source (they are never published), and a module list would
# have to be edited every time a module is added. This file is what makes that cheap — it drops
# everything the build does not need, so adding a module stays free and no stale output leaks in.

.git
.gitignore

# Maven / Quarkus build output — regenerated inside the build stage, and ~79 MB of it here. Copying
# it in would also risk a stale target/ shadowing what the stage compiles.
**/target
**/target-ide

# Local env / IDE cruft
.env
.idea
.vscode
.sdkmanrc

# Docs and the docker/ dir itself: nothing in the build reads them, and keeping them out means
# editing the Dockerfile or a README does not bust the `COPY . .` layer.
*.md
docker
